# Git: always commit and push

After completing any substantive code change in this repo:

1. Commit without asking for permission first.
2. Prefer working on `main`. If on a feature branch, still push that branch.
3. Push to `origin` immediately after every successful commit (`git push -u origin HEAD` when needed).
4. Skip secrets, credentials, `.env*`, and build logs (`nextbuild*.log`, etc.).
5. Use a concise commit message focused on why.
6. Never force-push to main. Never amend commits that are already pushed.
7. If there is nothing meaningful to commit, do not create an empty commit.
